rows-ambiguous-declaration = ambiguous effect-row declaration `{ $name }`
rows-captured-variable-needs-owner = the captured row variable `{ $var }` needs its lexical owner
rows-no-binder-identity = an effect row has no binder identity
rows-variable-no-owner = the row variable `{ $var }` has no lexical owner
rows-ambiguous-call = ambiguous lexical occurrence of an effect-row call
rows-call-no-owner = a call has no lexical effect-row owner
rows-kernel-name = `{ $name }` is the kernel's own; a program uses it inside a function of the proof language
rows-undefined-name = `{ $name }` is not defined in the program
rows-unfollowed-call = cannot follow the effects of calling `{ $name }`
rows-unfollowed-row-variable = cannot follow the effects of the row variable `{ $name }`
rows-unfollowed-expression = cannot follow the effects of an applied expression
rows-unfollowed-call-in = cannot follow the effects of calling `{ $name }` in `{ $owner }`
rows-unfollowed-row-variable-in = cannot follow the effects of the row variable `{ $name }` in `{ $owner }`
rows-unfollowed-expression-in = cannot follow the effects of an applied expression in `{ $owner }`
rows-out-of-steps = the effects could not be followed within the analysis steps
rows-out-of-steps-in = in `{ $owner }`: the effects could not be followed within the analysis steps
rows-ambiguous-function = ambiguous lexical occurrence of function `{ $name }`
rows-ambiguous-call-owner = ambiguous lexical owner of an effect-row call
rows-ambiguous-constructor-owner = ambiguous lexical owner of a constructor call
rows-writes-type-arguments = the row of `{ $name }` writes type arguments ({ $written }); a row names effects without them
rows-writes-type-arguments-instances = the row of `{ $name }` writes type arguments ({ $written }); a row names effects without them; write `∀ A. { $head }(A)` for every instance
rows-undefined-effect = the row of `{ $name }` names `{ $effect }`, which is not a declared effect; check the spelling or import it
rows-function-in-row = the row of `{ $name }` names `{ $effect }`, which is a function, not an effect; a row lists the effects a body may perform, and a function is called, so write the effects it performs (or leave it out) instead
rows-may-perform = `{ $name }` may perform { $effect } but its row is {"{"}{ $row }{"}"}
rows-extern-effects = an extern can perform only wait; wrap other effects in a tauto function
rows-unhandled-top-level = unhandled effect { $effect } at the top level
rows-entry-top-level = the top level performs { $effect } beside an entry (`main` or `test`); a module's top level only says which entries it has, so put this in the entry's body
rows-import-top-level = the top level of an imported script performs { $effect }; an import brings declarations and the statements of the script's top level are not run, so put this in a function there, or do not import the script
rows-module-top-level = the top level of a module performs { $effect }; a file of a tote's sources is a module, whose top level only says which entries it has, so put this in a function, or in the body of an entry (`main` or `test`)
rows-type-error = type error: { $message }
rows-value-performs = a function value may perform { $effect } but its type permits {"{"}{ $row }{"}"}
rows-value-performs-spawn = a function value may perform { $effect } but its type permits {"{"}{ $row }{"}"}; a task runs apart from the handlers around its `spawn`, so its handler goes in the task's body: `spawn(() => handler(f))`
rows-js-callback-effect = a callback through a JavaScript host frame cannot perform { $effect }, which may resume more than once; keep reusable continuations in Nib
rows-extern-closure-effect = a closure passed to an extern cannot perform { $effect }, which may suspend
rows-arm-not-direct = the arm of { $op } performs { $effect }, which is not direct
rows-undeclared-row-variable = the row variable `{ $var }` is not declared; write `<!{ $var }>`
rows-nested-callable = cannot follow nested callable effects
rows-row-stored-in-value = cannot follow an effect row stored in a value
rows-erase-bounds = cannot erase the bounds of a polymorphic function value
rows-erase-callback = cannot erase the callback capabilities of a host function value
rows-function-value-required = cannot follow the effects of a function value required by its type
rows-value-required = cannot follow the effects stored in a value required by its type
rows-mutable-callback-row = a mutable host callback needs an explicit effect row
rows-not-in-bound = { $effect } is not in { $name }, which bounds { $var }
rows-not-direct = { $effect } is not direct but { $var } is direct
rows-resumes-many = { $effect } resumes ω but { $var } is <=1
rows-unverified = the rows found for { $name } do not follow the effect-row rules
rows-unverified-top = the rows found for this top-level value do not follow the effect-row rules
rows-placement-arm-answers-only = an arm of `{ $op }` only answers where the value goes: write its body as `k(e)`, where `e` performs nothing
rows-row-hole = the row of `{ $name }` is `!?`: it is not written yet
